# Customer Churn Analysis

## Project Overview
This project analyzes customer data to understand why customers leave a company. It uses Python libraries to clean data, perform analysis, and generate visualizations.

## Objectives
- Clean and prepare customer data.
- Calculate the customer churn rate.
- Analyze churn based on gender, contract, and payment method.
- Compare monthly charges and customer tenure.
- Generate graphs and an analysis report.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn

## Dataset
IBM Telco Customer Churn Dataset.

## Project Structure
```text
Customer-Churn-Analysis/
│
├── data/
│   └── customer_churn.csv
│
├── output/
│   ├── cleaned_data.csv
│   ├── churn_report.txt
│   ├── churn_distribution.png
│   ├── gender_churn.png
│   ├── contract_churn.png
│   ├── payment_churn.png
│   └── monthly_charges.png
│
├── main.py
└── README.md
```

## How to Run
1. Install the required libraries:
   `py -m pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn`
2. Run the program:
   `py main.py`

## Expected Outcome
The project produces a cleaned customer dataset, a churn analysis report, and graphs that help identify customer churn patterns.

## Conclusion
This analysis helps understand customer churn behavior and identify factors that may influence customer retention.